{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"318364c2cd1a746c6f9438575e7727960e4fe1119e286ba2f84caf847f5a03fb","packTokens":3215,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1196,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1418,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":34,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using their Folio3 Google account, with employee profiles and vehicle details populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking with a single action and view its status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can schedule or cancel parking releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can view availability and claim released parking on a first-come, first-served basis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and generate and email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"When an employee with multiple registered vehicles claims temporary parking, which vehicle's plate should be authorized for that day's allocation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The employee selects one registered vehicle when claiming; only that plate is authorized for the allocation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which timezone defines “today,” the 30-day scheduling window, the daily release time, and Monday-morning report scheduling?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the office's local timezone for all date boundaries and scheduled times.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the system choose the assigned parking floor when it automatically allocates a claimed space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Choose a floor with the most remaining capacity, using a consistent tie-break when floors are equally available.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Which sources should provide the employee, vehicle, and parking-assignment records, and how should existing records be loaded?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the corporate directory for employee identity and an administrator-maintained parking/vehicle roster for assignments, initially loaded from existing records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How long should release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history be retained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply Folio3's existing records-retention policy to these histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"If a dedicated holder arrives in a vehicle with a permanent parking sticker after releasing their space and another employee has claimed it, which access outcome should apply?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Honor the permanent sticker holder's entry; the temporary claimant may be denied if the released space is occupied.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Which dates count as working days for the default dedicated-parking availability and related utilization scenarios?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat Monday through Friday as working days, without excluding holidays.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What parking information should security guards be able to access beyond the indicator result at the entrance?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only use the indicator; do not provide guards with a product screen or parking records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The application will be available on both iOS and Android platforms.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: The product shall be one responsive web app with layouts for phone, tablet, and desktop; pages shall avoid horizontal overflow at representative widths and narrow layouts shall use touch-sized controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 22 requirements proceed together as one run, or should the scope be reduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 22 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"If an entrance check fails because the camera, plate recognition, network, or indicator is unavailable, should the vehicle be held for manual verification or denied entry until service is restored?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Deny entry until service is restored; do not provide a manual-verification path.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the app ensure an employee can access only their own profile and vehicle data?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require the signed-in Folio3 Google identity to match the corporate email used to retrieve the profile, and restrict employee and vehicle data to that employee (with administrators retaining their authorized access).\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"If a permanent-sticker holder enters using a space that was released and allocated temporarily, what should happen to the temporary claimant’s authorization?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat the permanent holder’s detected entry as use of that space, cancel the temporary allocation, and deny the temporary claimant authorization for that space.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict sign-in to Folio3 Google Workspace accounts and show returning employees their dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Match each employee’s signed-in identity to their corporate email for self-service profile lookup, restrict employee and vehicle data to that employee, and allow administrators access to other employee records only as authorized; source identity from the corporate directory and parking assignments and vehicle details from the administrator-maintained roster initially loaded from existing records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Require employees without dedicated parking and without a registered vehicle to register at least one license plate before claiming; allow one or more plates with optional make, model, and color, and activate each plate immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Treat Monday through Friday, including holidays, as working days for default dedicated-parking availability and utilization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Allow a dedicated parking holder to release today’s assigned space in one action, reject duplicate releases, and expose space status as Reserved, Released, or Claimed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Allow dedicated parking holders to schedule one or more releases up to 30 calendar days ahead and display saved releases on a calendar.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Allow a holder to cancel a scheduled release only before its space is claimed, and record scheduling and cancellation events.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Use 8:00 AM as the default daily release time and let an administrator configure it in the office’s local timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Evaluate today, the 30-day scheduling window, daily release cutoffs, and weekly report scheduling in the configured office-local timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Make scheduled releases and same-day releases made before the daily release time claimable at that time, and make same-day releases made after that time claimable immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Show available-space counts and allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee whose claim is accepted, allowing each space to be claimed only once.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Require temporary-parking claimants to select one registered vehicle, authorize only that vehicle’s plate for the allocation, and assign a floor with the most remaining capacity using a consistent tie-break.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When spaces become available, email eligible employees without dedicated parking using a fixed-template message.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Reject employee cancellation of temporary parking claims in Phase 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"For car-plate detections reported by the existing entrance LPR camera, verify the plate against an active temporary allocation for the office-local date, request green-indicator activation only for valid authorization, and record the attempt’s date, time, plate, verification result, and entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Record permanent-sticker vehicle detections for utilization, bypass temporary authorization and entry blocking for those vehicles, and cancel a temporary allocation when its space is entered by its permanent holder, so subsequent verification denies the temporary claimant authorization for that space.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"On camera, plate-recognition, network, or indicator failure, or an unreadable plate, record unsuccessful verification, keep green authorization off, and deny entry until service is restored without offering manual verification.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Record an Unused Dedicated Parking event for each working day when a dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry was detected, and an Unused Temporary Parking event when the claimant’s selected vehicle was not detected entering on the claim date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Generate a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office timezone containing dedicated employees who neither released nor used their parking, temporary claimants who did not use their parking, daily and weekly statistics, total released spaces, total temporary claims, and an overall utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Email each weekly utilization report to designated stakeholders using the configured recipient list, and permit only authenticated parking administrators to update that list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Do not create automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on parking utilization in Phase 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Retain release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history according to Folio3’s existing records-retention policy.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Build one responsive web app for phone, tablet, and desktop; avoid horizontal overflow at representative widths and use touch-sized controls on narrow layouts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L3 ears] REQ-15 needs exactly one \"shall\"\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}